    `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36` OF
        `the year of Article 26(5) runs from the day the document is provided or retained`,
        `promptness under Article 26(6) is a judgement the caller supplies`,
        `only a purpose within Article 6(1)(c) counts under Article 28(1)(a)`,
        `the list of appealable decisions in Article 33 is closed`,
        `a decision of the tribunal is appealed to the court only on the ground in Article 35(1)`,
        `an appeal time limit under Article 36(2) runs from the notice of the decision`,
        `the day of service is not counted in a period fixed by a notice`,
        `calendar months`,
        `the year of Article 26(5) ends on the anniversary of the day it starts`,
        `a year of Article 26(5) from 29 February ends on 28 February`,
        `Article 29(1) requires both consents`,
        `the day of the anchor is not counted in an appeal time limit`,
        `any applicant for registration or registered charity is excluded from appealing under Article 33(5)`,
        `the Commissioner's belief alone is the ground under Article 27(1)`,
        `only a notice under Article 27(1)(c) or (d) may require a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced`,
        `Article 33(2)(a) reaches a deregistration granted on the charity's own application`,
        `a person falls within Article 26(2)(b) only if a governor while the entity was registered`,
        `each ground of Article 33(5) must hold at both times`,
        `the registered charity of Article 26(4)(a) is a charity registered now`

